---
description: Physics reconstructions from reference videos: measurement, solvers (ODE, FEM, CFD), verification, Blender bakes
globs: **/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Copy this file into your project's `.cursor/rules/`. Install the skill too (Cursor reads `~/.cursor/skills`,
`~/.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills`), so the rule can point at it.

- Use the `video-to-physics` skill: scaffold a case with `scripts/v2p.py new`, route the phenomenon with
  `references/physics-routing.md`, and follow the phases in `references/workflow.md`.
- Label every parameter measured, declared, assumed or fitted; never fit to a generator's defects.
- Benchmark solvers on closed forms first; converge on three resolutions; check budgets.
- Bake solver output through files (`deformation.npz`, tracer PNGs) and check the evaluated Blender result against
  them; build checkpoints with `v2p.py checkpoint` from frozen copies.
- Verify with an independent implementation and negative controls before calling anything verified.
